  "final_span": ". Human life can live only when society holds on to Christian tradition,\" Orban said hours after religious leaders converged in Rome for the annual overnight retreat of Cardinals marking the start of their new five-year terms run by Francis, who has said the Catholic Church&apos;s future depends on the faithful remaining connected to their tradition.\n\"Hearts may harden, but they can always soften. The tide can change...I am full of confidence. It is in your power to reverse negative trends,\" Francis said during his homily for the Mass.\nCardinal Timothy Dolan of New York criticized what he perceived as the decline in Catholic education, highlighting that about two-thirds of Americans baptized as infants from more modest economic backgrounds lack any formal education from Catholic institutions.\n\"Shocked? Sorry? Not much,\" said Massimo Faggioli, a professor of theology and religious studies at Villanova University in Pennsylvania. \"These in a sense are two themes of Pope Francis: Entropy, decay and the climate change for causes. These are recurring themes of pope, and no one can interpret it otherwise or accuse the pope, at least not in a way that gives the impression to be untruthful because he&apos;s citing a study of French historians one of the authors is working for the Catholic newspaper. These are not unreliable studies. The Pope is very much aware of the differences: There are differences, not nearly the Catholic intellectuals have been so focused for the last 40 years.\"\nThe report states that Francis will pursue a previous decision to invite Protestant church leaders to write an ecumenical note and cite a study by scholars in the Sunday letter.\nAfter a weekend at the isolated summer palace near Rome, where they get their formal attire and a ceremonial sword for a ritualistic papal coronation, the cardinals will participate in a live televised discussion at the Vatican on Friday, fulfilling their mainly ceremonial duties before the 